.TH BOSWAS-MEDIA-PLAYER 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-media-player \- play music and videos
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-media-player
.RI [ FILE | FOLDER | URL ]...
.br
.B boswas-media-player
.BR \-\-backend\-info " | " \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-media-player
is the music and video player of Boswas OS.
.PP
Files, folders, playlists (M3U, M3U8, PLS) and
.B http
or
.B https
addresses given on the command line are played, in the order given; a folder
stands for the media files in it and below it, in natural name order.
Without arguments the window opens with the play queue of the last run, the
last track loaded and paused where it was left.
.PP
Only one instance runs per session.
A later start hands its arguments to the running instance, which adds them
to the end of its play queue and comes to the front.
It has one window, as the media player of Windows has: there is one play
queue, and one player answers the media keys and the shell's media controls.
A start with
.B \-\-new\-window
is handled like any later start.
.PP
What can be played depends on the multimedia backend of Qt that is
installed (FFmpeg on Boswas OS); see
.BR \-\-backend\-info .
A file that cannot be played is skipped, and a message says which one.
.SS The window
.TP
.B Home
What was played recently, and buttons to open files, a folder or an address.
.TP
.B Music library
The music under the user's Music folder and the folders added in Settings,
as songs, albums and artists, from the tags of the files (ID3, Vorbis
comments, MP4 and RIFF INFO tags).
Covers come from the picture embedded in a file, else from
.BR cover.jpg ,
.BR folder.jpg ,
.B front.jpg
or
.B album.jpg
(also PNG and WebP) in its folder.
The folders are read in the background; an index is kept so that a later
start reads only new and changed files.
Symbolic links to folders and hidden files and folders are not followed.
.TP
.B Video library
The videos under the user's Videos folder and the folders added in Settings,
with a picture taken from each video when the backend can decode it.
.TP
.B Play queue
What is being played, in order.
Drag an item, or press Alt+Up and Alt+Down, to move it; Delete removes it.
.TP
.B Playlists
Playlists can be created, renamed, reordered, deleted, imported from and
exported to M3U, M3U8 and PLS files.
.TP
.B Settings
Library folders, whether videos resume where they were stopped, and the
playback device.
Theme and accent colour follow the desktop.
.PP
The bar at the bottom shows what is playing and holds the controls: previous,
play or pause, next, shuffle, repeat (off, all, one), the position with the
time under the pointer, volume and mute, playback speed (0.25 to 2 times),
the audio, subtitle and video tracks of the media when it has several, the
mini player and full screen.
In full screen the controls and the pointer hide while a video plays.
.PP
A network address is contacted only when the user opens it; while it plays
it is marked as a network stream.
.SS Desktop integration
The player is on the session bus as
.B org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.boswas\-media\-player
(MPRIS 2.2: the interfaces
.B org.mpris.MediaPlayer2
and
.BR org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.Player ),
so that the media keys, the quick settings and the lock screen can show and
control it.
The length of a track inside the
.B Metadata
property is sent as a 32-bit integer when it fits into one, and as a 64-bit
integer otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-backend\-info
Print the containers and codecs the multimedia backend reports, and exit.
The list is what Qt knows by name; the backend may play more.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of the command line and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Space, Ctrl+P|Play or pause
Ctrl+Right, Ctrl+Left|Next, previous
Right, Left|Forward, back 10 seconds
Ctrl+Up, Ctrl+Down|Volume up, down
M|Mute
Ctrl+H, Ctrl+T|Shuffle, repeat
F11, F, double click|Full screen (Escape leaves it)
Ctrl+M|Mini player
Ctrl+O, Ctrl+Shift+O, Ctrl+U|Open files, a folder, an address
Ctrl+F|Search the library
Ctrl+N, F2|New playlist, rename the open playlist
Alt+Left|Back
F5|Read the library folders again
Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Q|Close
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.MediaPlayer/settings.json
Library folders, volume, speed, playback device.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.MediaPlayer/playlists/*.m3u8
The playlists.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.MediaPlayer/
The play queue and position
.RB ( queue.json ),
recently played media, where each video was stopped, the library index
.RB ( library.json )
and the window size.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/com.boswas.MediaPlayer/
Covers and video thumbnails; can be deleted at any time.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/user\-dirs.dirs
Where the Music and Videos folders are (xdg\-user\-dirs).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, also when the arguments were handed to a running instance;
2 for a wrong command line; 4 when started as root, which is refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas\-photos (1),
.BR boswas\-camera (1),
.BR xdg\-user\-dirs\-update (1)
